      "side": 1,
      "message": "If 4KB processes keep BPF ring buffers, I think the 4KB and 8KB rings that `ringbuf_map_alloc()` now allows deserve a comment here. With a single data page, its second mapping in the `vmap()` starts 16KB after `rb-\u003edata`, so `rb-\u003edata + size` isn\u0027t an alias of `rb-\u003edata` as the comment above describes.\n\nAs far as I can see it still works: a record that wraps is written and read linearly from its header (`__bpf_ringbuf_reserve()` returns `hdr + 8` unmasked, and libbpf reads `len_ptr + 8`), `2 * size` fits in the page, and `ringbuf_map_mmap_slices()` maps it linearly too.\n\nCould you add a short note next to the `DIV_ROUND_UP()`, and mention the 4KB and 8KB rings in the commit message?",
