      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:57:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If these mappings stay, could the per-4KB insert be shared rather than open-coded here? The same `vmalloc_to_page()` plus `vm_insert_page_slice(..., offset_in_page(kaddr) \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_4KB)` loop is in `array_map_mmap_slices()` (aosp/4367949), and aosp/4368031 adds another copy to `remap_vmalloc_range_partial()`.\n\nOnly picking `kaddr` for the consumer, producer and data offsets is specific to the ring buffer. A helper in mm/ that maps vmalloc memory at `kaddr` into a 4KB VMA at `addr` would keep the slice handling out of `kernel/bpf/`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "845c5dc307c604d3166d3a2980919275d648fd11",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
