      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:57:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is the case I asked about on aosp/4367599: with libbpf\u0027s 4KB layout, the producer page at file offset 4KB and the data at 8KB both map slice 0, while `vma_slice_offset()` gives their addresses slices 1 and 2. So unlike the array map, the slices really can\u0027t follow the address here.\n\nI\u0027m worried about the code that still works the slice out from the address, though. As far as I can see, `__access_remote_vm()` (aosp/4368035) and `process_vm_readv()` (aosp/4312492) still do that at the top of the chain, so a debugger reading `producer_pos` through `ptrace()` or `/proc/pid/mem` would get offset 4KB of the producer page instead.\n\nWould failing the `mmap()` with `p3s_4k_unsupported()`, as aosp/4368077 does for the tracing ring buffer, be an option? That would leave 4KB processes without BPF ring buffers, since user space can\u0027t consume them without `mmap()` since only system processes can access these in Android.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "845c5dc307c604d3166d3a2980919275d648fd11",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
