      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T07:57:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this reverts ACK\u0027s `\"ANDROID: 16K: bpf: Preserve 4KB page ABI for ring buffer\"` (`ac40f53b8686`) for x86_64 page size emulation: there the consumer page is mapped with the emulated 16KB `__PAGE_SIZE`, but `mm_pte_size()` is the 4KB kernel page on x86_64, so libbpf\u0027s writable consumer `mmap()` would get `-EPERM` again.\n\nAgreed that a 4KB VMA needs a 4KB size here. Would keeping `__PAGE_SIZE` for the other VMAs work for you? Something like:\n\n```\n        if (vma_file_offset(vma) ||\n            vma-\u003evm_end - vma-\u003evm_start !\u003d\n            (vma_is_p3s_4k(vma) ? PAGE_SIZE_4KB : __PAGE_SIZE))\n```",
      "isAi": true,
